  "idea": "Cursor vs GitHub Copilot: which AI coding assistant writes better software",
  "text": "Cursor vs GitHub Copilot: which AI coding environment actually makes you ship software faster? Relying on simple inline autocomplete leaves developers copy-pasting code across fragmented terminal windows. Standard Copilot extensions only read open tabs, missing database schemas and complex project-wide dependencies. Cursor indexes your full repository, enabling multi-file refactors and automated terminal debugging in Composer. You build production features twice as fast.",
